  "why_scout_cares": "Piece-as-input at its purest: each of the 40 pieces has a unique binary pattern of bumps molded into its base; the board reads the bump contacts to identify the piece and its position in a single action, and enforces hidden state by only revealing ranks during combat. A genuinely distinctive sensory-board interaction with no coordinate keypad. DEFERRED 2026-09-16: zero freely-licensed images on Commons (only auction-site/all-rights-reserved photos). Revisit if a CC/PD photo of the board or a piece's bump-pattern underside surfaces.",
